   "type": "payment.succeeded",
   "created": 1768435200,
-  "data": { "paymentId": "pay_123", "amountCents": 12500, "currency": "USD" }
+  "data": {
+    "paymentId": "pay_123",
+    "amountCents": 12500,
+    "currency": "USD",
+    "customer": { "email": "ana@example.com", "cardLast4": "4242" }
+  }
 }
 ```
 
 `type` is one of `payment.succeeded`, `payment.failed` or `refund.created`.
 `data.amountCents` is a positive integer number of cents, `data.currency` an
-ISO 4217 code, and refunds may carry a free-text `data.reason`. Acme retries a
-webhook until it gets a 2xx, so the same `id` can arrive more than once.
+ISO 4217 code, and refunds may carry a free-text `data.reason`. Payment
+events carry the cardholder in `data.customer`, which we pass on in the
+`payments.<status>` message. Acme retries a webhook until it gets a 2xx, so
+the same `id` can arrive more than once.
 
